course: dictionary
lesson: 11092
title: Many jobs for one small word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word what is small, but it has several jobs. It can ask a question: «What is that?» It can ask which one or which kind: «What colour is it?» The words next to what show you which job it is doing.
explain: What can also mean «the thing that». «Tell me what you saw» means tell me the thing that you saw. Try swapping in the thing: «Tell me the thing that you saw». If it still makes sense, then what is doing that job.
explain: What can show surprise too. «What a big dog!» means how big the dog is, and your voice goes up with wonder. The exclamation mark is a clue that the speaker is excited or amazed.
explain: Be polite with what. Saying just «What?» can sound blunt, so say «Pardon?» if you did not hear. «What do you say?» is a polite reminder, like the one Sam's mum gave him about saying thank you.
fact: What is a word that can ask a question, as in «What is that?»
fact: What can mean «the thing that», as in «Tell me what you saw».
fact: «What a big dog!» uses what to show surprise, so it is an exclamation.
fact: «The kind words protect feelings, but you still need to know what really happened» uses what to mean «the thing that».
fact: Saying just «What?» can sound rude, so «Pardon?» is the politer choice.
exercise: «Tell me what you saw.» What does what mean here? | A question about a number | The name of a place | *The thing that | A shout of surprise
exercise: «What a big dog!» What is what doing in this sentence? | Asking which one | Counting the dogs | Saying sorry | *Showing surprise
exercise: «What colour is it?» What does what ask about? | The time | *Which colour | How far away it is | Who owns it
test: Sam's mum says «What do you say?» What is she reminding Sam to do? | Tell her the time | Count the presents | Go to bed | *Say thank you, to be polite
test: You did not hear what your friend said. Which is the more polite thing to say? | What? | *Pardon? | Whatever! | Speak up now!
exam: Which of these uses what to ask a question? | «What a big dog!» | «The kind words protect feelings» | *«What is that?» | «Tell me what you saw»
